But spec says "either both the current and the next old elements are null, or the current element equals the next old element."

Thus: (this.get(i) == null && \old(this.get(i+1)) == null) || this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i+1))).

Need to ensure safe when this.get(i) null; calling equals would NPE. So need to guard.

Thus final assert:

assert (index >= 0 && index < \old(this.size())) => \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size())-1; ( (this.get(i) == null && \old(this.get(i+1)) == null) || (this.get(i) != null && this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i+1)))) );

